From 375b43ff9df31eb95964b5ff4ecc549ed33f7dd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ientzy <ientzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:53:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Flash Next: output head with an 8-bit screen

NINFER_FLASH_HEAD_SCREEN=1 makes an 8-bit copy (Q8_G32_FP16) of the BF16 output
head when the program starts. A round of up to 16 columns whose rows have no
grammar mask and no penalty projects the copy, bounds its error per row
(row error norm times the column norm, plus BF16 rounding) and computes from
the BF16 head only the rows that can be among the 20 largest of a column;
sampling never reads further. Other rounds keep the full head.

NINFER_FLASH_HEAD_SCREEN=check runs both heads and counts top-20 rows the
screen left out, values that differ and columns with another first token.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
